# Corvidinho bot-VM env — copy to ~/.config/corvidinho/env (the updater's CORVIDINHO_ENV_FILE)
# or a systemd EnvironmentFile (mode 600); NEVER commit real values. A .env in the checkout
# root is also auto-loaded by Bun for processes started there (bridge, doctor, watch, daemon);
# with --project <path> the .env files in <path> are loaded instead (CLI-5). Never loaded by
# spawned agents (bun --no-env-file).
# Full checklist: docs/DISCORD-GO-LIVE.md
# When READY-FOR-SECRETS: request token via CoS/Leif secure room (never chat paste).

# --- Required to connect (DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN wins when both are set) ---
# DISCORD_TOKEN=
# DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=

# --- Required non-empty channel allowlist (comma-separated snowflakes) ---
# Empty = refuse start (default-deny; not Merlin BASIC).
# DISCORD_CHANNEL_IDS=
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_ALLOW_CHANNELS=

# --- Optional user/role gates: both empty = anyone in an allowlisted channel; once set, only listed users / role holders + the owner. Deny lists always win ---
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_ALLOW_USERS=
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_ALLOW_ROLES=
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_DENY_CHANNELS=
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_DENY_USERS=
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_DENY_ROLES=

# --- Allowlist file (preferred on bot VM) ---
# CORVIDINHO_ALLOWLIST_FILE=~/.config/corvidinho/allowlist.toml
# A leading ~ or ~/ is the bot's HOME (not ~user); any other path is used as
# written. See allowlist.example.toml. A file that cannot be read or parsed
# refuses start (bridge, watch, daemon) and every gate refuses — never an
# env-only fallback.

# --- Preferred: guild-scoped slash overwrite (DISCORD-4 / REQ-discord-016) ---
# Guild PUT of the nine commands + clear globals (kills duplicate /agents from old bots).
# Also the only guild discord-user-lookup searches (IDENTITY-5 / DISCORD-13; unset = it refuses).
# DISCORD_GUILD_ID=
# Then: bun src/cli.ts discord register-commands
# Or restart: bun src/cli.ts discord bridge

# --- Dry-run (no live Discord connect / no REST post; still needs any non-empty DISCORD_TOKEN value + channels) ---
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_DRY_RUN=1

# --- GitHub token: typed reads, github watch, /work draft PRs, public-repo checks for non-owner chat ---
# (GITHUB_TOKEN wins when both are set)
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# GH_TOKEN=

# --- GitHub allowlists (default-deny; union with [github] in the allowlist file; deny wins) ---
# CORVIDINHO_GITHUB_ALLOW_REPOS=      # OWNER/REPO or OWNER/* ; comma/space-separated
# CORVIDINHO_GITHUB_ALLOW_ORGS=
# CORVIDINHO_GITHUB_ALLOW_USERS=      # WATCH: empty = every event refused
# CORVIDINHO_GITHUB_DENY_REPOS=
# CORVIDINHO_GITHUB_DENY_ORGS=
# CORVIDINHO_GITHUB_DENY_USERS=
# CORVIDINHO_GITHUB_DRY_RUN=1         # GitHub write plugins: no live API call

# --- GitHub WATCH poll (docs/WATCH.md) ---
# CORVIDINHO_WATCH_USERNAME=          # login to listen for (alias: GITHUB_WATCH_USERNAME)
# CORVIDINHO_WATCH_INTERVAL_MS=60000  # min 30000
# CORVIDINHO_WATCH_MAX_TRIGGERS=5     # max agent spawns per poll cycle
# CORVIDINHO_WATCH_DRY_RUN=1          # echo agent; no spawn
# CORVIDINHO_WATCH_SPAWN_LOG=         # default <data dir>/watch-spawn.jsonl

# --- Optional rate limits + mute seed (DISCORD-6; no secrets) ---
# Defaults: window 60000ms, max 10 messages per user. Per-user only.
# DISCORD_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=60000
# DISCORD_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=10
# Optional JSON level→max override (2 = every non-owner caller, 3 = the owner); keep the single quotes:
# DISCORD_RATE_LIMIT_BY_LEVEL='{"2":10,"3":30}'
# Seed muted user snowflakes (in-memory; comma-separated):
# DISCORD_MUTED_USER_IDS=

# --- Durable owner = the only ADMIN (IDENTITY-1/2/3; overrides allowlist [owner] per field) ---
# Owner is ADMIN unless muted/deny-listed; empty = nobody is ADMIN (default-deny).
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_ADMIN_USERS / CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_ADMIN_ROLES are ignored (ADMIN is owner-only;
# the bridge and doctor warn when they are set).
# CORVIDINHO_OWNER_DISCORD_ID=
# CORVIDINHO_OWNER_GITHUB_LOGIN=   # @mentions only; on GitHub the owner is matched by [owner] github_id in the allowlist file (IDENTITY-7.a)
# CORVIDINHO_OWNER_DISPLAY=

# --- Optional confused-deputy strict mode (DISCORD-8 / Merlin) ---
# When 1/true, discord-post-message outside a bridge-started run (no acting Discord user)
# requires --requesting-user-id. Bridge runs always check the acting user.
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_REQUIRE_REQUESTER_CHECK=1

# --- Optional SAFE-1 / SAFE-5 (docs/DISCORD-GO-LIVE.md E.3 / E.7) ---
# Dangerous plugin names allowed non-interactively (comma/space-separated). An entry
# lets `corvidinho plugins run` and the /work draft-PR step use the tool, and offers it
# to the model in the owner's (ADMIN) runs and local task run; never to non-owner chats,
# WATCH or schedules. shell-exec and node/python/cargo-exec are never offered from here.
# e.g. git-commit,git-push,github-pr-create lets /work open draft PRs (owner only), and
# also lets the owner's runs commit, push and open PRs themselves.
# CORVIDINHO_ALLOWLIST=
# HMAC key for the tamper-evident audit chain; same value for every process on one data dir.
# CORVIDINHO_AUDIT_HMAC_KEY=


# --- LLM for task run: the model you configure (AGENT-13) ---
# There is no built-in default model: with no usable model set, every run (CLI, Discord,
# WATCH, schedules) fails with a "No model provider is configured" notice, and the bridge,
# `github watch`, the daemon, `task run`, /status and doctor say so (AGENT-10).
# CORVIDINHO_LLM_MODEL is `kind:model`, kind = openai | ollama | anthropic; a bare name (or
# an unknown prefix such as qwen3:30b) is OpenAI-compatible. All kinds use the
# OpenAI-compatible chat API. A comma list is accepted; only its first entry is called for
# now (fallback to the next one is not built yet).
#   openai:    CORVIDINHO_LLM_BASE_URL (default https://api.openai.com/v1) and
#              CORVIDINHO_LLM_API_KEY (or OPENAI_API_KEY)
#   ollama:    OLLAMA_HOST (default 127.0.0.1:11434); no key
#   anthropic: https://api.anthropic.com/v1 with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# Tier tool|code: interruptible plugin tool loop (AGENT-3/5). read = chat only.
# Dangerous plugins are left out of the task run tool catalog unless CORVIDINHO_ALLOWLIST
# names them (SAFE-1 / CLI-3; docs/DISCORD-GO-LIVE.md E.3).
# CORVIDINHO_LLM_MODEL=openai:gpt-4o-mini   # or ollama:qwen3:30b, anthropic:<model>
# CORVIDINHO_LLM_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=                    # fallback if CORVIDINHO_LLM_API_KEY unset
# CORVIDINHO_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OLLAMA_HOST=127.0.0.1:11434
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Images the agent opens with files-read (e.g. Discord attachments, DISCORD-9) go to the
# model as image parts; a model without vision gets a text note instead (one retry after an HTTP 400/404/413/415/422).
# CORVIDINHO_LLM_TIER=tool           # read | tool | code (AGENT-5)
# Optional model per tier (AGENT-5): each falls back to CORVIDINHO_LLM_MODEL. Same
# kind:model form; e.g. a local ollama: model for read, a stronger one for code.
# CORVIDINHO_LLM_MODEL_READ=
# CORVIDINHO_LLM_MODEL_TOOL=
# CORVIDINHO_LLM_MODEL_CODE=
# Optional (SESSION-5): the model's context window in tokens. Discord and WATCH
# conversations are condensed when the prompt reaches ~80% of it; the task and
# latest instruction stay word for word. Default 8192; minimum 1024.
# CORVIDINHO_LLM_CONTEXT_TOKENS=8192
# Optional daily spend cap (SAFE-8): USD over a rolling 24h across every task run on
# this box. At 80% you get one warning per crossing; a call that would pass the cap is
# not sent and the run stops and asks the owner (Discord ping) how to continue. An
# unpriced model also stops and asks while it is set. Unset = no cap. `doctor` and
# Discord `/status` show spend vs the cap. Restart the bridge/daemon after changing it.
# CORVIDINHO_DAILY_SPEND_CAP_USD=5

# --- Optional corvidinho bin override (defaults to <projectRoot>/src/cli.ts) ---
# Always bun-invoked when the path ends in .ts (never posix_spawn .ts alone).
# CORVIDINHO_BIN=

# --- Optional SESSION durable store (SQLite; align MEMORY path) ---
# Default data dir: ~/.local/share/corvidinho/  (DB: corvidinho.db)
# CORVIDINHO_DATA_DIR=
# Soft TTL ms for Discord and WATCH sessions (clamped to 30–60 minutes; default 45m):
# CORVIDINHO_SESSION_TTL_MS=2700000

# --- Optional nightly backup of that DB (OPS-1/2, docs/DAEMON.md "Nightly backup") ---
# Absolute local directory, outside any git repo (snapshots hold private notes).
# Unset = no backup (`doctor` says so). From 03:00 local time the bridge or daemon
# tick writes one consistent snapshot a night (mode 0600, keeps the newest 7) and
# once a week restores the newest into a temp dir to check it. A failure is logged
# and the owner is pinged once per failure streak in the /announce channel.
# Restore: `corvidinho backup list`, `corvidinho backup restore <snapshot> <target>`.
# Restart the bridge/daemon after changing it.
# CORVIDINHO_BACKUP_DIR=/var/backups/corvidinho

# --- Optional SESSION-WORKTREE base dir (#58) ---
# Default: sibling `.corvid-worktrees` next to each project working dir.
# WORKTREE_BASE_DIR=/workspace/.corvid-worktrees
